## Integrated Metadata Sources

| Provider | Purpose | API Endpoint / Method | Credentials |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| **Spotify Web API** | Track, album, and artist metadata | `https://api.spotify.com/v1/search` | Client ID & Client Secret |
| **iTunes Search API** | Track metadata fallback | `https://itunes.apple.com/search` | None (Public JSON) |
| **Last.fm API** | High-resolution artist photography | `ws.audioscrobbler.com/2.0/?method=artist.getinfo` | API Key |
| **Deezer API** | High-quality album cover artwork | `https://api.deezer.com/search` | None (Public JSON) |
| **YouTube Music** | Raw audio stream extraction | `yt-dlp` stream extraction | Optional `cookies.txt` |
| **Genius Lyrics** | Plain and synchronized lyrics | `genius-lyrics` client | Access Token |

---

## Audio Source Matching Strategy

The scraper matches metadata to audio streams by constructing targeted search queries:

1. Query string: `<Artist Name> - <Track Title> Official Audio`
2. Prefers YouTube Music streams over user-generated video uploads for higher bitrate consistency (`itag 251` Opus or `itag 140` AAC).

---

## Dedicated Provider CLI Commands

CLI commands allow executing ingestion for a specific metadata provider:

- **Spotify-First (`npm run spotify`)**: Ingests metadata 100% from Spotify Web API (`npm run spotify "https://open.spotify.com/track/..."` or `npm run spotify "Artist - Title"`).
- **Deezer-First (`npm run deezer`)**: Ingests metadata 100% from Deezer API (`npm run deezer "https://www.deezer.com/track/..."`).
- **Last.fm-First (`npm run lastfm`)**: Ingests metadata 100% from Last.fm API (`npm run lastfm "Artist - Title"`).
